  "claim_ceiling": "GDT635 gives a concrete predictive working model for strictly token-initial p/s/r/l on the already allowed 179-page scope: p=pulvis, s=semen, r=radix and l=lignum. Exact head deletion yields 760 bodies, 144 shared and 24 four-way; five complete paradigms give all 20 attested forms concrete class, dry, moist, material or portion readings, and ten matched spans receive complete practical translations. Initial, standalone, internal and terminal signs remain separate, and p/s versus r/l retain distinct placement subclasses. Historical technical manuscripts show that these four categories coexist with quality and degree architecture, but do not identify Voynich glyphs as Latin initials. This is a replaceable working theory, not a solved language, phonetic key or manuscript-wide plaintext.",
